# data: 195MB download + ~450MB cache, fetched by the setup step in README
data/
starter/
kuairand-starter-kit.zip

# Run outputs. The per-iteration logs and the scripts the agent wrote are graded deliverables,
# so runs from the current architecture are kept -- r27 onward, which are the runs whose brief
# and knowledge base carry no human findings, and which the ablation table in DEVPOST cites.
# Earlier runs (r1-r26) used the prior-laden prompt and are excluded; the prompt itself is kept
# in archive/ instead. Score blobs (*.npy, ~1.4MB each) are excluded everywhere.
runs/*
!runs/r96/
# the epsilon/N convergence sweep: three --patience 999 curves run to the 50-script cap so
# that no candidate N is censored by the stop rule. The logs and the agent's scripts are the
# evidence; the numbers drawn from them live in reports/convergence_sweep/.
!runs/convergence_sweep/
# the KuaiRand-1K bonus run behind RUN_REPORT_1K.md (logs only; its 532MB of scores,
# submission CSV and cached artifacts stay out).
!runs/r38_1k/
runs/*/scripts/*
!runs/*/scripts/*.py
*.npy
# model checkpoints the agent caches between iterations via RUN_ARTIFACTS: regenerable
# intermediates, 11MB in one run. The scripts that write them are kept; the weights are not.
runs/*/artifacts/
# a submission CSV is 5.9MB; the run that produced the submitted one is identified
# in RUN_REPORT.md, and the file itself is kept once at the repo root
runs/*/submission.csv

# 5.9MB of scores; the hand-tuned blend it came from is research/blend_model.py and the
# number it scored is cited in DEVPOST -- the CSV itself adds nothing a reader can check
research/*.csv
# r26 predates the decontaminated prompt, is referenced nowhere, and the r1-r26 runs that
# produced it are excluded above -- shipping its scores would contradict that
submission_fallback_r26.csv

# The rules above are written as runs/*/... and so miss runs nested one level deeper, such as
# runs/convergence_sweep/curve_1/. These repeat them at any depth so a nested run cannot smuggle
# in a 4.9MB submission CSV or a cache of model weights.
runs/**/artifacts/
runs/**/submission.csv
runs/**/scripts/**
!runs/**/scripts/*.py

blend/artifacts/
checkpoints/
components.npz

# local run driver: sources .env and loops the ladder. The protocol it encodes -- sequential
# execution, eps/N left at the run_agent.py defaults, s<slots>_r<repeat> naming -- is documented
# in reports/slot_ladder/README.md, so the repo keeps the method without shipping the script.
run_slot_ladder.sh

# The pre-decontamination prompt and knowledge base, the v1 writeup, and the AliCCP pipeline
# from the original problem statement. Kept locally as provenance; not shipped. NOTE: DEVPOST.md
# cites archive/proposer_v1_human_priors.py and archive/papers_v1_human_priors.json as the
# record of what was removed -- those citations do not resolve in a clone.
archive/aliccp/

# Anchored to the repo root. Written bare as `scripts/` it matched EVERY directory named
# scripts at any depth -- including runs/*/scripts/ -- and since a negation cannot re-include
# a file whose parent directory is excluded, `!runs/**/scripts/*.py` could not save them. The
# agent's own per-iteration scripts are a graded deliverable; no new run would have shipped one.
run_1k.sh
RUN_REPORT_1K_test.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.env

# local interpreter for runs; see requirements.txt for the pins
.venv/
